      "created_at": "2023-12-14T20:42:41Z",
      "updated_at": "2023-12-14T20:42:41Z",
      "body": "+1\r\nIn my use case, I am checking for some kind of cancellation condition during task runs and, based on that, I need to be able to cancel (fast-forward) the queue if the condition is true. The problem is that this queue needs an interval cap, which is still applied during fast-forwarding, leading to a considerable delay before the queue is flushed.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
