      "created_at": "2025-07-07T08:16:28Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-07-07T08:16:28Z",
      "body": "My use-case would be to bolt in a PID-controller on API endpoints returning 429 with no explicit ratelimits specified in the documentation or endpoints that allow burst-like behavior. The only thing required for this would be to control `#intervalCap` property of `PQueue` at runtime (Updating that would be up to a task function wrapper/error handler and be outside of PQueue code). Currently this is doable with a PNPM patch.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
